-- The middle file of a chain of three: it imports
-- ok/section-given-import-contract-def.l4, has a section GIVEN of its own, and
-- has three contracts that use the imported one: `both sides` names it as an
-- operand of RAND, `bob first` has it as a HENCE, and `plain mid` names it as
-- an operand of RAND and reads no section GIVEN of its own, so it is not a
-- closure for an importer, and is evaluated only where it is traced.
-- Each stops, in this file and in whatever imports it, in whatever position it
-- is used, if the operand is not applied (smucclaw/l4-ide#1118).
-- ok/section-given-import-contract-chain.l4 imports this one.

IMPORT `section-given-import-contract-def`

§ `Bob's side`
    GIVEN bobdl IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 10

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`both sides` MEANS
    `pay leg`
    RAND
    (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN bobdl)

#TRACE `both sides` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`bob first` MEANS
    PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN bobdl
    HENCE `pay leg`
    LEST BREACH BY Bob BECAUSE "late"

#TRACE `bob first` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 3
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 9
  WAITUNTIL 30

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`plain mid` MEANS
    `pay leg`
    RAND
    (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 12)

#TRACE `plain mid` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30
